```

Actually, looking at `_timer.py`: `__enter__` calls `start()` and returns `self`, so `timer_1 is timer_0`. Then `__exit__` calls `stop()`. Then `timer_1.start()` starts it again (both are the same object). Then `timer_0.start()` tries to start an already-running timer → raises `TimerError`.

